<title>SWEDEN: Two Americans, one Briton win Nobel Chemistry Prize.</title>
<headline>Two Americans, one Briton win Nobel Chemistry Prize.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Americans Robert Curl and Richard Smalley and Briton Sir Harold Kroto won the 1996 Nobel Chemistry Prize, the Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The academy said the prize was awarded for their discovery in 1985 of fullerenes, new forms of the element carbon in which the atoms are arranged in closed shells.</p>
